-- What's new: the latest versions' notes for the settings panel.
-- GENERATED by tools/changelog2lua.js from CHANGELOG.md; do not edit by hand.
local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.0.16", text = "Aura corners that use the whole frame, a threat number that knows you're the tank, and a long list of fixes.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffDispel icons:|r a friend with a Magic, Curse, Disease or Poison debuff shows the icon. Enemies never do.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r tank a few mobs in a group. The ones you hold are green, the ones you lost are red.\n• |cffffffffBuffs and debuffs Above or Below the Frame, or in one corner only:|r smaller icons or a wider frame fit more on a line.\n• |cffffffffMeter:|r use Create a New Tab, then check the new tab's list in a fight.\n• |cffffffffLoot window:|r Growth on Up, then drag the window and loot again.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffBuffs and debuffs in a corner:|r with nothing in the corner across from them, they use the whole width of the frame.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager:|r the Essential and Utility icons and Tracked Buffs fill from the middle. Pick another |cffffffffGrowth|r in Edit Mode to change it.\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r the name colours from before 7.0.15 are back.\n• |cffffffffSkin Item Slots:|r Colour by Rarity starts at green. Grey and white items have the bronze border.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r its colours follow your Role.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed and loot rolls:|r they show above the bags and other windows.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffCenter Spell Name|r (off): the spell's name in the middle of the cast bar.\n      - In Edit Mode, in every frame's Cast Bar section\n      - For the Player Cast Bar, in its Look section\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Crowd control and defensive icons have their own |cffffffffAura Icon Shape|r, |cffffffffAura Swipe|r and |cffffffffAura Timer|r. Until you pick something, they follow the other auras.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r |cffffffffGrowth|r (Down) and |cffffffffRow Order|r (Top to Bottom). By Xentinus.\n• |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack:|r each soul bag in your bag slots gets its own section.\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldown Manager|r\n• |cffffffffGrowth|r (From the Middle) for the Essential and Utility icons, in Edit Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Bar:|r Friends and Guild. They count who is online. Point at them to see who.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r colours:\n      - Tank: green while you hold the mob, orange when you're losing it, red when you lost it\n      - Damage & Healer: green while you're safe, red when it's on you\n      - The green is your |cffffffffYou Hold It|r colour\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r names have FlareUI's colours again, and titles and guilds have a colour of their own.\n• The target arrows push the quest mark and the other marks beside the plate out of the way.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffShow Spell Pushback|r comes after Edge Glow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffReverse Bag Fill|r works with Category Rows. Each section fills that way under its header.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• The gear menu's Show New Window is now called |cffffffffCreate a New Tab|r, because that's what it does.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffZone Headings|r greys out with Sort By on By Level or By Progress, where there are no headings.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Pet Reminders are for a missing or dead pet. The one for a hurt pet never showed, so it's gone.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• A Lua error with buffs and debuffs in places that share an edge, such as Above the Frame and Above the Frame, Left.\n• Buffs and debuffs in a corner wrapped at the middle of the frame, even with nothing in the other corner.\n• Dispel icons showed where you can't dispel:\n      - Players of the other faction who aren't flagged for PvP\n      - Bleeds\n      - Party and raid members under Mind Control\n• |cffffffffThreat Text:|r 0% on a mob only you have threat on, where the game hides the numbers.\n• The interrupt colour counted an interrupt your stance or shield didn't allow.\n• \"Interrupted by\" stayed on the cast bar for your next target.\n• |cffffffffName Above Frames:|r names in other alphabets showed as boxes.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Rows of buffs and debuffs fit one icon less since 7.0.9.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r a red 0% on a mob only you have threat on, where the game hides the numbers.\n• A plate reused in a fight could show dispel icons on an enemy.\n• Plates kept the wrong type when you changed sides, as in a duel.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffUpdate Spell Ranks|r left out the controller bars.\n• The range colours also changed buttons that aren't FlareUI's.\n• |cffffffffSharp Outline:|r text that stayed on screen after its bar faded out should go now. We couldn't see it ourselves, so tell us if it stays.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• Party buttons kept old names after the group changed in a fight.\n• Some spell ranks were wrong right after logging in.\n• Party spells in a sub-radial now spread over your group.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• The separate threat window didn't follow the meter's Opacity.\n• Pointing at the separate threat window didn't bring back a faded meter.\n• |cffffffffBar Texture:|r it could go back to Blizzard's after a while. We couldn't find the cause, but it now puts itself right.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• Share Quest could be blocked when a fight started with the menu open.\n• Item buttons could use the wrong quest's item, and took clicks while faded out.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• A farming HUD that takes the map no longer gets our click area, fading and hidden dots.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Short buffs counted as running out too early, such as Battle Shout.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• Accept Summons no longer takes a summons out of the starting area or into a scenario. You answer those.\n\n|cffe6cc99Languages|r\n• |cffffffffHungarian:|r two lines had wrong letters. By Xentinus." },
    { version = "7.0.15", text = "A hotfix for the Lua error when you change target in a fight (our own doing, from 7.0.14), plus a few fixes and small additions.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffDispel icons:|r change target in a fight with debuffs up. Friends show the icons, enemies don't.\n• |cffffffffRaid Manager:|r join a group in and out of a fight, with it hidden.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r with Smooth Animated Bars.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the colours in |cffffffffName Only Mode|r.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r titles and guilds take the name's colour, and names take the colours Blizzard gives them. Colours you picked yourself stay.\n• |cffffffffRaid Manager:|r if you hid it but play without our Action Bars, it's hidden now.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r with a font picked for Item Level, the BoE mark takes it too.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffCopy From|r, in Plate Setup: puts another unit's whole setup on the one you're editing. Undo Changes takes it back.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r Blizzard's colours for names, titles and guilds.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffOnly Mana Power Bars|r (off) works in every party style, Forever Style too.\n• A |cffffffffFrame Style|r you pick waits for the reload. By mateuszmalek.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• The BoE mark takes the Item Level font, in the bags and the loot window.\n\n|cffe6cc99Languages|r\n• |cffffffffRussian:|r shorter names for the Nameplates tabs and Plate Setup.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• A Lua error each time you changed target in a fight.\n• The player and target frames got shorter when you switched |cffffffffFrame Style|r and back. By mateuszmalek.\n• |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r left out the |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r bar.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• The target arrows hitched at each end of their bounce.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• A hidden |cffffffffRaid Manager|r still showed with Action Bars off, or when you joined a group in a fight." },
    { version = "7.0.14", text = "The blocked bag clicks: potions, recipes, crates and gear that the game refused to use after a visit to the bank. It's the worst bug FlareUI ever had.\n\n|cffffffffA HUGE thank you to parchinskiy,|r who hunted it down test after test until it had nowhere left to hide. Awesome work!\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffBags:|r use items after you visit the bank, with |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r and |cffffffffKeyring in Backpack|r on. If one is still blocked, send us what |cffffd100/fui errors|r shows.\n• |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack:|r move, split, search and use items in its section.\n• |cffffffffBank:|r buying bank slots, and opening it twice in a row.\n• |cffffffffController:|r radials on your bar if you play on two computers.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r combo points with your own plate width.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r combo points follow the plate's width. A width of 150 looks as before. Wider plates get bigger points, narrower ones smaller.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r switching |cffffffffCombined Backpack|r in FlareUI's settings asks for a reload.\n• |cffffffffDispel icons:|r enemies' debuffs no longer show one on the target, focus and boss frames.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffNameplate Combo Points|r (off): combo points under your target, on Blizzard's own nameplates. It's on the Gameplay tab while FlareUI's Nameplates are off.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• |cffffffffPet commands|r (Attack, Follow, the stances and the rest of your pet's bar): first under Pet Spells.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Bigger maximum sizes: height 50, cast bar 40, buffs and debuffs 50, crowd control and defensives 60.\n• Plates grow and shrink smoothly with |cffffffffTarget Scale|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffFade Delay|r shows in Edit Mode with any Visibility while |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r is on.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• Items blocked after a visit to the bank:\n      - The crafting bag in the backpack no longer opens Blizzard's bag window. By parchinskiy.\n      - Keyring in the backpack: FlareUI cleans up after itself when it opens Blizzard's window.\n      - Bags that open with the character window or the guild bank no longer add to it.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• Radials on the controller bar broke when you played on two computers. They go by the radial's name now: give it the same name on both.\n\n|cffe6cc99Auras|r\n• Dispel icons showed on enemies' debuffs.\n\n|cffe6cc99Performance|r\n• |cffffffffMinimap:|r with the coordinates on the Info Bar, less memory while you stand still.\n• The language files are smaller: phrases nothing uses any more are gone." },
    { version = "7.0.13", text = "A fix for the battleground errors that came with 7.0.12, and a check of every part of FlareUI, with more than 50 fixes.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffBattlegrounds:|r tell us if you still see \"cannot be accessed while tainted\" errors.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r item clicks after a visit to the bank, with |cffffffffMove Any Window|r on.\n• |cffffffffGroups:|r party and raid frames, with |cffffffffAlways Show|r auras and after a /reload in a raid.\n• |cffffffffAction bars|r that fade to nothing: clicking, dragging spells and starting fights.\n• |cffffffffController, rogues and warriors:|r the radial in a fight, and |cffffffffKick Ready|r on your higher ranks.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffChat:|r windows keep 128 lines again. The 500 lines of 7.0.12 caused the battleground errors.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r with |cffffffffMove Any Window|r on, a bag's title only drags. The bag menu (Assign To, Ignore This Bag) opens with a left-click on the bag's icon.\n• |cffffffffAction bars:|r a bar faded to nothing, without Mouseover, takes no clicks, drags or tooltips. Its keys still work. In a fight it takes clicks, except on Never.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the game's own fades (distance, not your target) are off, so only FlareUI's options fade plates. Plates you leave to Blizzard lose them too.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r a dead mob's plate goes at once. A dead player's stays.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode layouts:|r in a layout where you never moved a frame, it can go back to the spot it has in another layout.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffMail Address Book:|r |cffffffffRemove from the List|r, in its menu.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r while you are the Master Looter, Blizzard's loot window takes over, with its assign menu.\n• |cffffffffCombine Empty Slots:|r free slots in a soul bag or another special bag are counted apart. Locked slots aren't counted.\n• |cffffffffDelete Junk When Full|r keeps:\n      - Soulbound greys worth nothing, and pieces of equipment sets\n      - Greys in bags set to ignore junk selling, and in special bags\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldowns|r\n• |cffffffffEnable Blizzard Cooldown Manager|r tells you why when it can't change.\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• |cffffffffFlareUI Settings|r in a frame's dialog asks you to save or revert your Edit Mode changes first. It used to drop them.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• Errors in battlegrounds, blamed on other addons.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffDelete Junk When Full|r deleted junk for loot you couldn't take yet: locked, yours to hand out, or double-clicked. It also ignored room in the crafting bag and keyring.\n• |cffffffffPlain Empty Slots|r hid the padlock on locked slots.\n• |cffffffffLoot Roll Window:|r a roll stays while the game still has it open, and never shows an impossible time.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Errors in fights with |cffffffffTint Health|r on By Health, and on enemy players in battlegrounds.\n• A tapped mob no longer keeps a threat colour or number.\n• |cffffffffKick Ready|r no longer marks friends' casts.\n• No debuff type icon on enemy plates.\n• The target arrows no longer move in steps.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffKick Ready|r works for rogues from level 26 and warriors from 32, on nameplates too.\n• Pointing at a faded frame's buffs and debuffs brings the frame back.\n• |cffffffffTotems:|r with Aura Timer on None, the time is hidden.\n\n|cffe6cc99Party and raid frames|r\n• |cffffffffAlways Show|r auras from other players show.\n• Everyone's buffs show when they share a place with the debuffs.\n• A /reload in a raid made up to twice the frames it needed.\n• After quick group changes, a frame could show the wrong player.\n• Ready check marks no longer stay with the next player.\n• Blizzard's hidden party and raid frames no longer work in the background.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• Changes made before a fight, such as joining a group or looting potions, are there when it starts.\n• A radial that was empty opens once it has something to show.\n• Macros that share a name each run their own.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Demonic Sacrifice only shows with Demonic Pact.\n• Reminders on Mouseover appear.\n• |cffffffffNever Remind Me|r stays with its own custom reminder when you remove another.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• A separate threat window froze while the meter was faded out.\n• |cffffffffReport to Chat|r on Deaths sends the time of each death.\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldowns|r\n• The icons no longer jump after an |cffffffffIcon Shape|r change. By Nico-Mayer.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• The swing bar knows you are attacking after a /reload.\n• |cffffffffSeals:|r no gap beside the icon.\n• |cffffffffXP bar:|r a fight in Edit Mode shows the real bar.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• Edit Mode's Icon Size comes back after the map fades.\n• |cffffffffSquare:|r gathering addons see the map under your mouse again.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• Scrolling and then clicking opened the wrong quest.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• |cffffffffAccept Summons:|r a summon you declined no longer makes it take the next one at once.\n• Changing a setting on the vendor's Buyback tab could buy back the wrong item.\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings|r\n• In Edit Mode, a fight no longer takes your keys, and the dialog's X works.\n• |cffffffffReset FlareUI|r can still undo the nameplate and UI Scale settings FlareUI changed.\n• Long tab names no longer overlap.\n• Frames keep their spots in a third Edit Mode layout.\n• |cffffd100/fui errors|r counts repeated errors, and says more about blocked bag clicks." },
    { version = "7.0.12", text = "A clean-up of the chat, easier to spot elites in Modern Style, guild names on nameplates and spell ranks on the radials.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffChat:|r names, levels and web links on every kind of line, and replying to whispers with R, also in a boss fight.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r party spells while you're alone, with nothing targeted, next to a vendor.\n• |cffffffffModern Style:|r the gold and silver borders, and the level in front of the name above a frame.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffChat:|r only Alt+Up and Alt+Down go through the messages you sent, as in the default chat. The arrows alone no longer do it.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r with |cffffffffLevel Before Names|r on, far more people show a level.\n• |cffffffffModern Style:|r target, focus and boss frames get a gold border for elites and bosses, and a silver one for rares.\n• |cffffffffModern Style:|r with |cffffffffShow Level|r on, the level also shows in front of |cffffffffName Above Frames|r.\n• |cffffffffPet frame:|r the happiness icon beside it is as tall as the health bar.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r |cffffffffButton Names|r is now |cffffffffIcon Labels|r. Your choice is kept.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffShow Guild Name|r (off) for players in Name Only Mode:\n      - Set separately for enemy and friendly players\n      - Under the name, or under the title when Show Titles is on\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• |cffffffffShow Spell Rank|r (Off), for spells below your best rank:\n      - |cffffffffIn the Icon:|r the rank's number, at the top left\n      - |cffffffffIn the Label:|r after the name, like \"Frostbolt (Rank 2)\"\n      - |cffffffffBoth|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• A warning when another addon that changes the chat is running too, such as Prat or ls_Glass.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffModern Style, elites and rares:|r\n      - The skull is a third larger\n      - The borders follow the |cffffffffElite & Rare|r icon: turn it off to keep the normal border\n      - The threat glow still takes over while you have threat\n• |cffffffffModern Style, level above the name:|r on every frame with both options, except in FlareUI and Forever Style, which have a level disc.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• Each window keeps 500 lines to scroll back through (was 128). The Combat Log is unchanged.\n• Alt+Up goes back through your last 200 messages (was 50).\n• |cffffffffLevel Before Names|r uses the level the game sends with each player.\n• |cffffffffSave History:|r old lines no longer offer Report, because it could point at the wrong message.\n\n|cffe6cc99Languages|r\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r texts from 7.0.6 to 7.0.11. By Braincell1980.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffChat:|r web addresses can be clicked in community channels, Discord guild chat and party guide lines.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r |cffffffffSave History|r keeps your last 128 lines of conversation in each window. Loot messages used to push them out.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r |cffffffffSave History|r keeps Discord guild chat.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r |cffffffffCopy Chat|r shows Battle.net friends by name.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r with nothing targeted, a party spell you use alone goes to you. It went to the NPC in front of you.\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffName Above Frames|r shows over the elite dragon in FlareUI Style." },
}
